# Files excluded from the Vercel deployment upload.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# vercel.json builds every "*.{html,css,svg,png,jpg,jpeg,webp}" as a static
# asset, which silently published the test harness pages — for example
# https://moviezone.dev/tv-mode.browser.test.html was reachable in production.
# The harnesses are dev tooling: they load index.html in an iframe and POST to
# a /__results endpoint that only exists in the test runner, so on production
# they are dead weight that also exposes internal test wiring.
#
# These stay in the repo (they are wired into `npm test` and guard against real
# regressions) — they just stop shipping.

# Browser test harness pages
*.test.html

# Node test suites
*.test.js

# One-off verification scripts (carousel geometry, OTT ids, SEO SSR, TV perf…)
*-check.js

# TV performance baseline, only read by tv-perf-check.js
perf-baseline.json
